flowchart TB
    accTitle: Product X example of candidate values and selection
    accDescr: Three book-created Product X candidates receive illustrative values under an invented uncertainty-reduction criterion. Argmax carries the candidate with the greatest displayed value forward. The values are not probabilities, paper results, or evidence about the incident.

    subgraph CAND[Book-created candidate set]
      direction TB
      A[Inspect deployment metadata<br/>illustrative value: 0.80]
      B[Query database connectivity<br/>illustrative value: 0.60]
      C[Ask on-call engineer<br/>illustrative value: 0.45]
    end
    EVAL[Evaluation under an invented<br/>uncertainty-reduction criterion]
    MAX[Argmax selection]
    OUT[Carry forward: inspect deployment metadata]
    NOTE[Illustrative values only<br/>not probabilities or incident findings]
    A --> EVAL
    B --> EVAL
    C --> EVAL
    EVAL --> MAX --> OUT
    OUT -.-> NOTE

    classDef process fill:#EAF4FB,stroke:#1A4A8A,color:#1C1C1E,stroke-width:1.5px;
    classDef candidate fill:#F4F4F4,stroke:#888888,color:#1C1C1E,stroke-width:1.1px;
    classDef result fill:#EEF7EE,stroke:#27AE60,color:#1C1C1E,stroke-width:1.4px;
    class A,B,C,NOTE candidate;
    class EVAL,MAX process;
    class OUT result;
